 "notes": "Headline dark photon bound from the rapid cooling of Cas A (Eq. 37, epsilon*m_gamma' < 1.5e-8 MeV for m < Tc(n3P2) ~ 0.1 MeV; red region of Fig. 6, CCDK proton-singlet pairing model). Boundary traced pixel-wise from the full-resolution raster embedded in the e-print figure DPConstraints.pdf; axes calibrated from major tick marks (x: 214.15 px/decade anchored at 10^-2 eV; y: 171.04 px/decade anchored at 10^-3). Curve follows eps*m ~ 1.5e-2 eV at low mass, dips to eps ~ 1.1e-7 near m ~ 5e4 eV, and rises steeply at the m ~ Tc cutoff (~5e5 eV). The paper also derives a stronger but conditional dark photon bound from NS1987A (eps*m < 3e-9 MeV, Eq. 39, brown dashed in Fig. 6) and a U(1)_B-L bound e' < 5e-13 (Fig. 7); the Cas A dark photon bound is the one quoted first in the abstract and labeled the key result. Stellar-cooling bound: no DM density assumption, no explicit confidence level stated (0.95 entered as default).",
